    "q-6944": {
      "dom_id": "step-q6944",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Determine the equation of the line that passes through the points $(4,7)$ and $(5,17).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17-7}{5-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{1} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=10$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=10x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(4,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =10x+b \\\\ 7 & =10(4)+b \\\\ 7 & =40+b \\\\ 7-40 & =b \\\\ -33 & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the line is $y=10x-33.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
